        "step_id": 6,
        "message": "I\u2019ll inspect both full CT volumes, delineate findings that appear more likely tumor, and compare their anatomical locations across visits. I\u2019ll preserve review images and scripts alongside the masks, event file, and uncertainty report.\n"
      },
      {
        "step_id": 14,
        "message": "The scans have different coverage and slice spacing, so I\u2019m matching lesions by anatomy rather than raw slice numbers or world-coordinate offsets. The follow-up contains a prominent liver abnormality; I\u2019m reviewing its baseline counterpart and checking the rest of both volumes for smaller findings.\n"
      },
      {
        "step_id": 23,
        "message": "The chest and abdomen review has not shown a convincing extrahepatic mass so far. I\u2019m using narrower liver windows and adjacent slices to separate true low-density lesions from vessels and image noise, including subtle baseline findings.\n"
      },
      {
        "step_id": 35,
        "message": "A subtle right-liver lesion is visible at baseline in the same region as the much larger follow-up lesion. Several nearby dark structures trace into vessels on multiplanar views, so I\u2019m checking those carefully before assigning additional lesion IDs.\n"
      },
      {
        "step_id": 44,
        "message": "I found a second, small round liver focus on follow-up that does not trace into a vessel and has no convincing baseline counterpart. I\u2019m including it as a probable tumor candidate despite the limited contrast, while completing a systematic pass through the remaining anatomy.\n"
      },
      {
        "step_id": 57,
        "message": "The full-volume survey supports one baseline liver lesion and two follow-up liver lesions. The right-thigh skin/subcutaneous abnormality has a similar flat, scar-like appearance at both visits and is being excluded. I\u2019m now refining the lesion boundaries and checking the masks against the original slices.\n"
      },
      {
        "step_id": 70,
        "message": "The masks now capture the visible liver lesion boundaries, including the larger follow-up lesion where it reaches the liver surface. The correspondence is one persistent lesion plus one newly appearing small lesion. I\u2019m finishing the evidence report and validating voxel grids, affines, instance IDs, and JSON coverage.\n"
      },
      {
        "step_id": 75,
        "message": "Created all requested files in [/app/answer/](/app/answer/):\n\n- [Baseline mask](/app/answer/baseline_instances.nii.gz)\n- [Follow-up mask](/app/answer/followup_instances.nii.gz)\n- [Events](/app/answer/events.json)\n- [Report](/app/answer/report.md)\n\nResult: one persistent liver lesion and one newly appearing follow-up lesion. Grid, affine, and ID checks passed. Scripts and evidence views are preserved in `/app/work/`."
      }
